WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.177
Before Transformers became dominant, recurrent neural networks and LSTMs were common choices for sequence

00:00:07.177 --> 00:00:10.417
data. An RNN reads a sequence step by step.

00:00:10.417 --> 00:00:17.092
The hidden state from one position contributes to the next position, so the model naturally preserves order.

00:00:17.092 --> 00:00:24.922
LSTMs and related gated architectures improved the ability to keep useful information over longer sequences.

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:29.382
The difficulty is that the computation is still strongly sequential.

00:00:29.382 --> 00:00:34.542
Later steps depend on earlier steps, which makes training harder to parallelize.

00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:41.112
Long-range information can also become difficult to preserve through many recurrent transitions.

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:44.842
Transformers changed the organization of the computation.

00:00:44.842 --> 00:00:49.037
Instead of passing information only through a chain of hidden states,

00:00:49.037 --> 00:00:53.112
attention lets tokens interact more directly with other tokens.

00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:56.517
This does not mean RNNs suddenly became invalid.

00:00:56.517 --> 00:01:02.702
It means Transformers offered a more scalable way to model broad context and became especially effective when

00:01:02.702 --> 00:01:04.960
trained on very large datasets.
